# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Vim swap files
*.swp

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
vendor/

# unibuild image tars
*.tar

# binaries
dist/

# temporary files and dirs used while building images
temp/

# dir for test bundles
bundles/

# python-related directories
__pycache__/

# Artifacts leaked into the repo root by go-118-fuzz-build / the containerized
# OSS-Fuzz build. That build runs as root through a bind mount, so it both
# drops .a/.h files here AND leaves them root-owned, which silently made seven
# harness source files unwritable (found 2026-08-28). Never commit these.
fuzz_*.a
fuzz_*.h
*_fuzz.go
main.*.go

# Machine-generated fuzzing corpus. Go writes every coverage-interesting input
# here during a campaign -- currently ~4000 entries, almost all noise (one
# target alone accumulated 1301). The durable seeds live in f.Add() calls in
# the harness source, so nothing is lost by ignoring these.
#
# If a real crash reproducer is ever found, commit that one deliberately with
# `git add -f <path>`: a committed reproducer replays on every `go test` and is
# the regression guarantee worth having. Blanket-committing the coverage corpus
# is not.
**/testdata/fuzz/

# Orphaned output from an earlier, separate fuzz-orchestration run (2026-09-10),
# unrelated to the current suite.
logs/

# Scratch scripts left by automated edit passes.
rewrite_*.py
fix_*.py
